## 1. Architecture Overview

```
tests/sql/testcases/*.sql
        │
        │  parsed at pytest collection time
        ▼
tests/helpers/sql_test_parser.py   ←  SqlTestCase + SqlAssertion dataclasses
        │
        │  list[SqlTestCase] passed to
        ▼
tests/test_sql_runner.py           ←  @pytest.mark.parametrize generates 1 test per SQL case
        │
        │  uses
        ├──► tests/conftest.py      ←  db_conn (session) + clean_tables (per-test autouse)
        │
        │  executes body SQL + assertions via pyodbc against
        ▼
SQL Server 2022 (Docker / CI service)
        │
        ├── TestDB.dbo.STAGING
        ├── TestDB.dbo.STAGING_FOLDERS
        ├── TestDB.dbo.TARGET_FOLDERS
        ├── TestDB.dbo.HASH_REGISTRY
        └── TestDB.dbo.SYS_DELTA_LOG
```

**Key design principle:** Test authors write only SQL. Python is responsible for discovery,
execution, and reporting — no Python changes are needed to add a new test.

