## 7. Stored Procedures Under Test

### Database tables

| Table | Role |
|-------|------|
| `dbo.STAGING` | Parent table — auto-ID, required for FK integrity |
| `dbo.STAGING_FOLDERS` | Incoming raw data; `Is_Processed = 'N'` for unprocessed rows |
| `dbo.TARGET_FOLDERS` | Final destination — only new/changed rows land here |
| `dbo.HASH_REGISTRY` | SHA-256 fingerprint per unique row seen; keyed by `entity_name + row_hash` |
| `dbo.SYS_DELTA_LOG` | Audit log — one row per SP execution with all counters and status |

### `USP_DELTA_FOLDERS` — execution phases

| Phase | Code section | What happens |
|-------|-------------|--------------|
| 1 | Open audit log | `INSERT INTO SYS_DELTA_LOG … status='RUNNING'`; captures `log_id = SCOPE_IDENTITY()` |
| 2 | Acquire lock | `sp_getapplock 'USP_DELTA_FOLDERS', 'Exclusive'`; raises error if lock unavailable within 30 s |
| 3 | Build `#staging_hash` | Computes `SHA2_256(CONCAT_WS('\|', ISNULL(field, ''), …))` for each unprocessed row; assigns `ROW_NUMBER()` within each hash group |
| 4 | Count input | `input_row_count = COUNT(*)`; `rows_deduped = SUM(CASE WHEN rn > 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)` |
| 5 | Early exit | If `input_row_count = 0`: commit, update log to `SUCCESS` with all zeros, return |
| 6 | Mark unchanged | `UPDATE HASH_REGISTRY SET updated_datetime = @current_timestamp` for hashes that already exist (`rn = 1` only) |
| 7 | Insert new hashes | `INSERT INTO HASH_REGISTRY` for hashes not already present (`rn = 1` only) |
| 8 | Insert target rows | `INSERT INTO TARGET_FOLDERS` for rows whose hash was just inserted (`system_datetime < @current_timestamp` filter distinguishes new from pre-existing) |
| 9 | Retire stale hashes | `DELETE FROM HASH_REGISTRY WHERE updated_datetime < @current_timestamp` removes hashes not seen in this batch |
| 10 | Mark processed | `UPDATE STAGING_FOLDERS SET Is_Processed = 'Y'` for all rows in `#staging_hash` (new, unchanged, and deduped) |
| 11 | Commit + log | Commit transaction; update `SYS_DELTA_LOG` with final counters and `status='SUCCESS'` |
| CATCH | Error path | Rollback transaction; update `SYS_DELTA_LOG` with `status='FAILED'` + `error_message` |

### `USP_DELTA_MASTER` — behaviour

A pure orchestrator. Calls approximately 40 entity-level delta procedures in sequence.
Each call is individually wrapped in `BEGIN TRY … END CATCH` so a failure in one
sub-procedure is swallowed and execution continues to the next.

The master does **not** create its own `SYS_DELTA_LOG` entry — each sub-SP manages
its own audit log row.

