## 9. Test Case Reference — USP_DELTA_MASTER

All tests are in `tests/sql/testcases/test_usp_delta_master.sql`.

---

### TC01 — Master procedure executes without error

**Description:** `USP_DELTA_MASTER` completes successfully with no unhandled exception.

**Setup:** None — empty staging.

**Assertions (1):**

| # | Description | Expected |
|---|-------------|----------|
| 1 | USP_DELTA_FOLDERS logged at least one entry | `COUNT(*) >= 1` WHERE `entity_name = 'FOLDERS'` |

**Why it matters:** Baseline smoke test — confirms the master can be called at all.

---

### TC02 — Sub-procedure failures do not stop the master

**Description:** Non-existent sub-procedures (all 38 entities other than FOLDERS, which
do not exist in the test database) are silently swallowed via `TRY/CATCH`; `USP_DELTA_FOLDERS`
still runs and logs success.

**Setup:** None — empty staging; only `USP_DELTA_FOLDERS` is created in the test DB.

**Assertions (1):**

| # | Description | Expected |
|---|-------------|----------|
| 1 | USP_DELTA_FOLDERS logged a SUCCESS entry | `COUNT(*) >= 1` WHERE `entity_name = 'FOLDERS'` AND `status = 'SUCCESS'` |

**Why it matters:** Confirms the `BEGIN TRY … END CATCH` wrappers around each sub-SP call work
correctly. If a missing procedure caused the master to abort, `USP_DELTA_FOLDERS` would never run.

---

### TC03 — Master delegates to `USP_DELTA_FOLDERS` end-to-end

**Description:** When `STAGING_FOLDERS` has data, calling `USP_DELTA_MASTER` processes it
through `USP_DELTA_FOLDERS`.

**Setup:** 2 staging rows (`MASTER-F001`, `MASTER-F002`).

**Assertions (3):**

| # | Description | Expected |
|---|-------------|----------|
| 1 | Both staging rows were processed into TARGET_FOLDERS | `COUNT(*) = 2` |
| 2 | USP_DELTA_FOLDERS logged SUCCESS | Latest FOLDERS log `status = 'SUCCESS'` |
| 3 | rows_upserted is 2 | Latest FOLDERS log `rows_upserted = 2` |

**Why it matters:** End-to-end integration test through the master — confirms the delegation
chain works, not just that the master exits without error.

---

### TC04 — Master does not create its own `SYS_DELTA_LOG` entry

**Description:** `USP_DELTA_MASTER` is a pure orchestrator with no `INSERT INTO SYS_DELTA_LOG`
of its own. After calling it, no row with `entity_name = 'MASTER'` should exist.

**Setup:** None — empty staging.

**Assertions (2):**

| # | Description | Expected |
|---|-------------|----------|
| 1 | No log entry with entity_name = MASTER | `COUNT(*) = 0` WHERE `entity_name = 'MASTER'` |
| 2 | FOLDERS sub-SP was invoked and logged | `COUNT(*) >= 1` WHERE `entity_name = 'FOLDERS'` |

**Why it matters:** If the master ever starts creating its own log entries (e.g. after a
refactor), monitoring dashboards expecting only sub-SP entries would show unexpected rows.

