## 13. GitLab CI Pipeline

**File:** `.gitlab-ci.yml`

```yaml
stages:
  - test

sql-unit-tests:
  stage: test
  image: python:3.11-slim
  services:
    - name: mcr.microsoft.com/mssql/server:2022-latest
      alias: sqlserver
      variables:
        ACCEPT_EULA: "Y"
        MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD: "Str0ngPass!2024"
  before_script:
    - pip install -q -r requirements.txt
    - python tests/setup_db.py
  script:
    - pytest tests/ --tb=short --junitxml=test-results.xml --html=test-report.html --self-contained-html
  artifacts:
    when: always
    reports:
      junit: test-results.xml
    paths:
      - test-results.xml
      - test-report.html
    expire_in: 30 days
```

### Pipeline stages

| Stage | What happens |
|-------|-------------|
| SQL Server starts | Docker service `mcr.microsoft.com/mssql/server:2022-latest` spins up alongside the Python runner |
| ODBC driver installed | `apt-get install msodbcsql18` in the runner container |
| Python deps installed | `pip install -r requirements.txt` — installs `pyodbc`, `pytest`, `pytest-html` |
| DB bootstrapped | `python tests/setup_db.py` — polls for SQL Server readiness, creates `TestDB`, runs DDL |
| Tests executed | `pytest tests/ --junitxml=... --html=...` — runs all 25 SQL-driven test cases |
| Artefacts published | JUnit XML (test tab in MR) + HTML report (downloadable for 30 days) |

### Viewing results

- **GitLab MR → Tests tab** — pass/fail count per test case
- **GitLab MR → Artefacts → `test-report.html`** — full HTML report with assertion-level detail

