## 14. Environment Variables Reference

All connection settings can be overridden at runtime. Defaults match the Docker Compose setup.

| Variable | Default | Used by |
|----------|---------|---------|
| `DB_HOST` | `localhost` | `setup_db.py`, `conftest.py` |
| `DB_PORT` | `1433` | `setup_db.py`, `conftest.py` |
| `DB_NAME` | `TestDB` | `setup_db.py`, `conftest.py` |
| `DB_USER` | `sa` | `setup_db.py`, `conftest.py` |
| `DB_PASSWORD` | `Str0ngPass!2024` | `setup_db.py`, `conftest.py` |

**Override example (CI / custom SQL Server):**
```bash
DB_HOST=my-sql-server \
DB_PORT=1433 \
DB_NAME=MyTestDB \
DB_USER=sa \
DB_PASSWORD=MySecret! \
  python tests/setup_db.py && pytest tests/ -v
```
